RRuntimeError is a Python/rpy2 exception saying that the evaluation of R 
code was stopped because of an error.
That error is reported verbatim (as shown above) and is:
"density.default(list(4.52, 2.42, 4.5, 2.54, 9.79, 2.5, 3.96,  :
   argument 'x' must be numeric".

r.density(robjects.FloatVector(data_dict['Income']))
will likely work.


A system for guessing and converting python sequences could not make it 
in time for the release 2.0, but will be present in 2.1.



L.







